first i defined my new function in both the header file and camera.cpp. it takes the parameters of the camera position (cPos), where the camera is currently facing (front) and the world's up vector (worldUp). 
after that, i needed to calculate each coordinate axis manually. the forward vector (where the camera is facing) which is glm::normalize(cPos-front), since the camera looks at the negative z-axis. then i did the right vector, which is the cross product of the world up and the forward vector, which we again normalize. finally i do up vecotr by doing the cross product of the forward and right vectors.
after i had my coordinate axes, i can now make the view matrix, which i do by first making a 4x4 matrix of all 1's. then i assign each part of the matrix to go along with the example in the notes.  the final row makes sure the camera is always at the origin of it's coordanite system. finally, we return the matrix
